<div class="wrap section section--tight">
<h1>A tour of Deaftly</h1>
<p class="lede">Real screens from the app, in the order you'll meet them.</p>
</div>

<div class="wrap tour">
<section id="home-screen" class="tour-step">
<img src="/screenshots/hub.webp" width="390" height="844" loading="lazy" alt="The home screen. Under Show are Start typing and Use a template. Under Chat are Face to face and Side by side. Each has an information button.">
<div>
<h2>The home screen</h2>
<p>Everything starts here, in two groups. <strong>Show</strong> is for saying something once, clearly. <strong>Chat</strong> is for a conversation. Tap the information button on any option for a short explanation.</p>
</div>
</section>

<section id="templates" class="tour-step">
<img src="/screenshots/fill.webp" width="390" height="844" loading="lazy" alt="The Check in template: Hi! I'm deaf. I'd like to check in. My name is, then name and how to reply as highlighted gaps, with a Show button below.">
<div>
<h2>Templates</h2>
<p>Pick a message you use often, like Check in, Order food or At the doctor's. The parts that change are highlighted. Tap one to fill it in: choose from a list, type it, or read it with the camera. Then tap Show.</p>
</div>
</section>

<section id="type-and-show" class="tour-step">
<img src="/screenshots/type-and-show.webp" width="390" height="844" loading="lazy" alt="Type and show, with the message: Could I have a table for two by the window, please? We are both vegetarian. A Show button sits at the bottom.">
<div>
<h2>Type &amp; show</h2>
<p>For anything you haven't saved as a template. Type what you want to say, then tap Show to put it on the whole screen.</p>
</div>
</section>

<section id="show" class="tour-step">
<img src="/screenshots/show.webp" width="390" height="844" loading="lazy" alt="A message filling the screen in very large text, with highlights on the filled-in parts. Below it, a Continue as chat button and the hint Swipe down to go back.">
<div>
<h2>Show</h2>
<p>Your message fills the screen in large, clear text. Switch between black on white, white on black and yellow on black to suit the light. If they want to reply, tap Continue as chat.</p>
</div>
</section>

<section id="face-to-face" class="tour-step">
<img src="/screenshots/face-to-face.webp" width="390" height="844" loading="lazy" alt="Face to face. The top of the screen shows the conversation upside down, for the person opposite. At the bottom, the typing field with Table for two and a Continue side by side button.">
<div>
<h2>Face to face</h2>
<p>Hold your phone and type. The keyboard faces you and your words face the other person, upside down from your side, so they read along as you type. When they want to reply, tap Continue side by side.</p>
</div>
</section>

<section id="side-by-side" class="tour-step">
<img src="/screenshots/side-by-side.webp" width="390" height="844" loading="lazy" alt="Side by side chat between Sam and a waiter, laid out like a script in two colours, with bold and highlighted words, a reply box, formatting buttons and a switch showing it's the waiter's turn.">
<div>
<h2>Side by side</h2>
<p>A back-and-forth on one phone. Each person's messages appear in their own colour, like a script. Flip the switch to change turns, and switch sides to match where you're standing. Add bold, italics and highlights, quote a message, or insert a template.</p>
</div>
</section>

<section id="camera" class="tour-step">
<img src="/screenshots/camera.webp" width="390" height="844" loading="lazy" alt="The camera reading a menu, with two lines picked: Lasagne 14.00 and Pasta arrabbiata 12.50. An Add to message button is below.">
<div>
<h2>Read text with the camera</h2>
<p>Point your camera at a menu, label or sign. Tap lines or drag across words to pick them, then add them to your message. Freeze the picture to make picking easier, and use the torch when it's dark.</p>
</div>
</section>

<section id="settings" class="tour-step tour-step--text">
<div>
<h2>Settings</h2>
<p>Set your name and colour for chats, choose light, dark or system appearance, pick the colours Show starts in, and bring back any built-in templates you've deleted.</p>
<p><a class="button" href="/download/">Get Deaftly for Android</a></p>
</div>
</section>
</div>
